sign-mldsa-not-supported: TPM2_Sign rejects ML-DSA keys with TPM_RC_SCHEME

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 3, "Signing and Signature
Verification", Table "Signing commands overview"):

  "(Pure) ML-DSA | Message (see Note) | Not supported | ..."

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 3, "TPM2_Sign"):

  "If inScheme is not a valid signing scheme for the type of keyHandle (or
  TPM_ALG_NULL), then the TPM shall return TPM_RC_SCHEME."

TPM2_Sign() does not support ML-DSA keys, so no signing scheme is valid for
them. Version 185 selects the NULL scheme for an ML-DSA key and goes on: it
checks the digest against the size of the NULL hash (TPM_RC_SIZE for any
non-empty digest), computes a hash-check ticket with a NULL hash for a
restricted key, and finally treats the digest as an external mu
(TPM_RC_EXT_MU without allowExternalMu, TPM_RC_VALUE for its size). The
patch returns TPM_RC_SCHEME + RC_Sign_inScheme for an ML-DSA key after the
x509sign check.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/Sign.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/Sign.c
index 7077c5a5..b5da25f4 100644
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/Sign.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/Sign.c
@@ -47,6 +47,15 @@ TPM2_Sign(Sign_In*  in,  // IN: input parameter list
         return TPM_RCS_ATTRIBUTES + RC_Sign_keyHandle;
     }
 
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // TPM2_Sign() with an ML-DSA key is "Not supported" (Part 3, Table "Signing
+    // commands overview"), so no signing scheme is valid for the key type
+    // (TPM_RC_SCHEME, Part 3, TPM2_Sign).
+#if ALG_MLDSA
+    if(signObject->publicArea.type == TPM_ALG_MLDSA)
+        return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_Sign_inScheme;
+#endif  // ALG_MLDSA
+
     // Pick a scheme for signing. If the input signing scheme is not compatible
     // with the default scheme or the signing key type, return an error. If a
     // valid hash algorithm is not specified, return an error.
